# T_SCRR: a saved user given a new password and a new full name, whose
# USER RESET is taken and whose USER SET is refused (102 naming
# FULLNAME, the test's answer): a box says the password was saved, then
# the refusal goes to the full name.  Ctrl-S again sends only the full name,
# the repetition of the password having been wiped with it; F3 on the
# list, answered No, stays, and answered Yes quits before the password
# screen.  The requests are checked by T_SCRR.
K DOWN ENTER PGDN UP
T pass99
K TAB
T pass99
K PGUP TAB CTRL-Y
T Otto Opstein Sr
K CTRL-S
S PWONLY
K ENTER
S REFUSED
K CTRL-S
S RESAVED
K F3
T N
K F3
T Y
